<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand also fell, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	18.37	    -158	    18.00     18.50</p>
<p>91-Day	18.95	    - 69	    18.80     19.00</p>
<p>182-Day     20.40	    - 16	    20.15     20.49</p>
<p>357-Day     20.24				20.20     20.30</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 21.16 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.50 bln pesos     3.12</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   2.67 bln pesos     3.34</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   1.81 bln pesos     2.26</p>
<p>357-Day     600 million pesos   1.31 bln pesos     2.18</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 2.76 on demand of 8.29 billion pesos compared with 5.53 the week before, on demand of 16.57 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   13 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    5 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   9 basis points</p>
<p>    357-Day			   6 basis points</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
